# project: mobile-app-launch
// First mobile app: MVP -> TestFlight beta -> App Store -> launch -> handover.

VAR beta_cycles = 0
VAR submissions = 0

-> build_mvp

=== build_mvp ===
Build the MVP: the smallest version of the app worth putting in testers' hands.
Done when the core flows work end to end on a real device.
+ [MVP is ready for testers] -> closed_beta

=== closed_beta ===
Closed beta via TestFlight: ship a build, collect feedback and crash reports, fix, repeat.
Done when the crash-free rate is above 99.5%.
~ beta_cycles += 1
+ [Crash-free rate is above 99.5%] -> app_store_submission
+ {beta_cycles < 4} [Iterate on beta feedback] ~loop~ -> closed_beta
+ {beta_cycles >= 4} [Four cycles and still below target] @human -> architecture_review

=== architecture_review ===
The hard conversation: is the app architecture actually sound, or are we polishing something structurally broken?
+ [Architecture is sound, keep working the beta] @human ~loop~ -> closed_beta
+ [Architecture needs rework, rebuild the app] @human ~loop~ -> build_mvp
* [Not worth saving, stop here] @human -> END

=== app_store_submission ===
Submit to the App Store for review. Rejections are expected: read the feedback, fix, resubmit.
~ submissions += 1
+ [Apple approved the app] -> launch_scheduling
+ {submissions < 3} [Rejected, fix and resubmit] ~loop~ -> app_store_submission
+ {submissions >= 3} [Rejected three times, something fundamental is wrong] @human -> rejection_escalation

=== rejection_escalation ===
Three App Store rejections means the problem is not cosmetic. Escalated to the project owner to decide the path forward.
+ [Address the fundamental issue and rebuild] @human ~loop~ -> build_mvp
* [Shelve the launch] @human -> END

=== launch_scheduling ===
The app is approved. Marketing picks the actual launch date; that is their call, not engineering's.
+ [Marketing confirms the launch date, go live] @human -> launch_monitoring

=== launch_monitoring ===
The app is live. Monitor crash rates, reviews, and support channels closely for one week.
+ [Serious incident, pull the app from the store] @human ~loop~ -> closed_beta
* [First week is clean] -> maintenance_handover

=== maintenance_handover ===
Hand the app over to the maintenance team: docs, dashboards, on-call. Project complete.
-> END
